  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q33-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "33",
    "prompt": "The ratio of the coefficient of $x^{r+2}$ to the coefficient of $x^r$ is $8:1$ in the expansion of $(1+x)^{20}$. Find $r$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$r=4$.\n\nForm $\\frac{\\binom{20}{r+2}}{\\binom{20}{r}}=8$ and simplify.",
      "worked": "The coefficients are $\\binom{20}{r+2}$ and $\\binom{20}{r}$, with $0\\le r\\le18$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\binom{20}{r+2}}{\\binom{20}{r}}&=8\\\\\\frac{20!}{(r+2)!(18-r)!}\\frac{r!(20-r)!}{20!}&=8\\\\\\frac{(20-r)(19-r)}{(r+2)(r+1)}&=8\\\\(20-r)(19-r)&=8(r+2)(r+1)\\\\7r^2+63r-364&=0\\\\7(r-4)(r+13)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThus $r=4$ or $r=-13$. Since $r$ is a non-negative integer, $r=4$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 70
  },
